From: Petr Štetiar <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
Date: Wed, 04 Nov 2026 07:58:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dm_exec: restore the FD output pointer NULL check

The broker copies the descriptor key and resource-limit flag from a
synchronous UDS response to optional output parameters. Since v11.0.4,
IsMatchingMsgId() compares the bool pointer fd_res_exceeded with true
instead of checking whether the caller supplied it. Ordinary output
addresses do not equal 1, so neither metadata field reaches the caller.

```text
src/core/dm_exec.c:2641:45: warning: comparison between pointer and integer
```

Restore the NULL check so both fields are copied when their output
pointers are provided. The flag's value must not decide whether its
output pointer is valid.

With file descriptor passing enabled, the native response probe supplies
key 42 and an exceeded flag of true. Before this change both outputs
stay at their initial zero values. With the NULL check they return 42
and true, and the pointer-comparison warning is gone.

References: PCF-2859, PCF-2860
Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://bitbucket.org/broadband-forum/obuspa/pull-requests/340]
Assisted-by: codex:gpt-6.1-sol:high
Fixes: acb8eabeb970 ("2026-06-05 v11.0.4: USP_ENDPOINT_ID environment variable")
Signed-off-by: Petr Štetiar <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>

---
 src/core/dm_exec.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/core/dm_exec.c b/src/core/dm_exec.c
index 9c00d0aaf7a0..4d840b468ea7 100644
--- a/src/core/dm_exec.c
+++ b/src/core/dm_exec.c
@@ -2638,7 +2638,7 @@ Usp__Msg *IsMatchingMsgId(dm_exec_msg_t *msg, char *msg_id, char *responder, Usp
 
 #ifdef FD_PASSING_EXPERIMENTAL
     // If source of message is UDS protocol - extract file descriptors key
-    if ((fd_key != NULL) && (fd_res_exceeded==true) && (pur->mtp_conn.protocol == kMtpProtocol_UDS))
+    if ((fd_key != NULL) && (fd_res_exceeded != NULL) && (pur->mtp_conn.protocol == kMtpProtocol_UDS))
     {
         (*fd_key) = pur->mtp_conn.uds.fd_key;
         (*fd_res_exceeded) = pur->mtp_conn.uds.fd_res_exceeded;
--
